---
const journey = [
  { stage: "Visual design", detail: "Learning craft, communication and visual problem solving." },
  { stage: "UX & product design", detail: "Moving from communicating information to understanding users, workflows and product problems." },
  { stage: "Startup product design", detail: "Learning to design with speed, ambiguity and limited resources." },
  { stage: "Darwinbox, early design team", detail: "Helping establish product design foundations while the company scaled from startup to unicorn." },
  { stage: "Enterprise product design", detail: "Complex workflows, business rules, permissions, configurations and global product requirements." },
  { stage: "Design leadership", detail: "Leading designers and product areas while influencing product direction and staying close to execution." },
  { stage: "AI & agentic product design", detail: "Applying years of enterprise systems experience to products that can understand intent, reason, act and collaborate with people." },
]
---

<section id="about" class="border-t border-[var(--color-border)] sec-y md:sec-y">
  <div class="container-pg">

    <!-- ── 01 Story ───────────────────────────────────── -->
    <p class="text-label mb-12 text-[var(--color-ink-3)]" data-reveal>01. About me</p>

    <div class="grid gap-16 md:grid-cols-[1.3fr_1fr] md:gap-16 lg:gap-24">

      <!-- Opening hook -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm mb-10 leading-tight" data-reveal data-delay="1">
          I found my way into
          product design
          by making things.
        </h2>

        <div class="space-y-6 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-ink-2)]">
          <p data-reveal data-delay="2">
            I started my career as a self-taught graphic designer and gradually found my
            way into UX and product design. Over the last 16+ years I've worked across
            visual design, startups, services and product teams, eventually spending
            nearly nine years designing enterprise HR technology.
          </p>
          <p data-reveal data-delay="3">
            I joined Darwinbox early in its journey and became part of the founding design
            team, helping establish the design foundations as the company grew from a
            startup into a unicorn. Since then my work has moved from individual product
            design into leading multiple product areas and helping teams solve
            increasingly complex problems.
          </p>
          <p data-reveal data-delay="3">
            Today I lead design across Time Management, Core, Payroll, Benefits,
            Extensibility and Workflows &amp; Journeys. Much of my work involves products
            with years of history, multiple user roles, business rules, configurations,
            permissions and dependencies. I enjoy getting into that complexity,
            understanding how the system actually works and finding ways to make the
            experience clearer.
          </p>
          <p data-reveal data-delay="4">
            My role has evolved from designing screens to shaping product direction,
            working with product and engineering leaders and helping designers navigate
            difficult product problems. I still like staying close to the work, whether
            that means mapping a workflow, questioning an interaction, reviewing a
            prototype or exploring a new product idea.
          </p>
          <p data-reveal data-delay="4">
            More recently I've been exploring AI-native and agentic experiences for
            enterprise products. I'm particularly interested in what happens when AI moves
            beyond chat and becomes part of real workflows, decisions and actions. I care
            about simple experiences, thoughtful product decisions and teams that
            understand the problem before jumping into solutions.
          </p>

          <!-- Links -->
          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 pt-4" data-reveal data-delay="4">
            <a
              href="/resume"
              aria-label="Résumé"
              class="roll-btn inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-[var(--color-border)] px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium text-[var(--color-ink)] no-underline transition-colors hover:border-[var(--color-ink)]"
            >
              <span class="roll" aria-hidden="true">
                <span class="roll-copy">Résumé ↓</span>
                <span class="roll-copy roll-copy--in">Résumé ↓</span>
              </span>
            </a>
            <a
              href="https://linkedin.com/in/kishuxer"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              aria-label="LinkedIn"
              class="roll-btn inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-[var(--color-border)] px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium text-[var(--color-ink-2)] no-underline transition-colors hover:border-[var(--color-ink)] hover:text-[var(--color-ink)]"
            >
              <span class="roll" aria-hidden="true">
                <span class="roll-copy">LinkedIn ↗</span>
                <span class="roll-copy roll-copy--in">LinkedIn ↗</span>
              </span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Career as evolution -->
      <div data-reveal data-delay="2" class="md:sticky md:top-24 md:self-start">
        <p class="text-label mb-8 text-[var(--color-ink-3)]">My career journey</p>
        <div class="space-y-6">
          {journey.map((step, i) => (
            <div
              data-reveal
              data-delay={String(Math.min(i + 2, 4))}
              class="border-l-2 border-[var(--color-border)] pl-5"
            >
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">{step.stage}</p>
              <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-ink-2)]">{step.detail}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ── 02 Beyond work ─────────────────────────────── -->
    <div class="mt-14 border-t border-[var(--color-border)] pt-12">
      <p class="text-label mb-8 text-[var(--color-ink-3)]" data-reveal>02. Still making things</p>

      <p class="max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-ink-2)]" data-reveal data-delay="1">
        I've always learned by making, a product concept, a visual experiment,
        a new tool I'm trying to understand. Curiosity is still most of how I work.
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>
